*> Implementation test (lane cmdfix): /locate structure answers on a freshly opened standard world before any chunk was generated by the main process
*> (the generation workers make the chunks, so the one-time setup of the generator, the climate points and the possible structure sets has not run): the
*> village (random_spread) and the stronghold (concentric_rings, 36-1 section 11 step 3) are found, and the answer is the one a world whose setup has run
*> gives. Needs the generated packs (CC_GENERATED_DIR): a pass without them.
 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. TEST-CMD-LOCATE-LAZY.
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 COPY TESTLIB.
 COPY CORESTATE.
 COPY COREAPI.
 COPY GENQUEUE.
 COPY CLIMATE.
 COPY STRUCTDATA.
 01 WS-ENV                 PIC X(1024).
 01 WS-DIR                 PIC X(1024).
 01 WS-FILE                PIC X(1100).
 01 WS-FILE-INFO           PIC X(16).
 01 WS-LINE                PIC X(768).
 01 WS-LAZY-V              PIC X(4096).
 01 WS-LAZY-S              PIC X(4096).
 01 WS-LAZY-T              PIC X(4096).
 01 WS-TEXT                PIC X(4096).
 01 WS-NUM                 BINARY-DOUBLE.
 01 WS-WORLD               PIC X(64) VALUE Z"build/core-test-world".
 01 WS-CREATED             BINARY-LONG.
 PROCEDURE DIVISION.
     MOVE "N" TO TL-MODE
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-ENV
     ACCEPT WS-ENV FROM ENVIRONMENT "CC_GENERATED_DIR"
     IF WS-ENV = SPACES
         MOVE "/tmp/cc-test/generated" TO WS-DIR
     ELSE
         MOVE WS-ENV TO WS-DIR
     END-IF
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-FILE
     STRING FUNCTION TRIM(WS-DIR TRAILING) "/vanilla-data/pack.mcmeta" X"00" DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-FILE
     CALL "CBL_CHECK_FILE_EXIST" USING WS-FILE WS-FILE-INFO
     IF RETURN-CODE NOT = 0
         MOVE "test cmd locate lazy no generated packs here, skipped" TO TL-CASE
         MOVE 1 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
         MOVE 1 TO TL-OBSERVED-N
         CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
         STOP RUN
     END-IF
     MOVE "T" TO TL-MODE
     CALL "TEST-SETTINGS" USING CORE-SETTINGS
     MOVE "standard" TO CS-WORLD-TYPE
     MOVE WS-DIR TO CS-GENERATED-DIR
     MOVE 2 TO CS-VIEW-DISTANCE
     MOVE "3" TO CS-SEED-TEXT
     MOVE 0 TO CS-HOSTILE-MOBS
     CALL "TEST-OPEN-WORLD" USING CORE-SETTINGS

     MOVE "test cmd locate lazy the opened world has not run its setup (no chunk made by this process)" TO TL-CASE
     DISPLAY "STATE setup-done " GQ-SETUP-DONE " cl-count " CL-COUNT " poss-done " SD-POSS-DONE " gate " SD-GATE-COUNT

     MOVE "locate structure #minecraft:village" TO WS-LINE
     CALL "TEST-RUN-CONSOLE" USING WS-LINE WS-LAZY-V
     MOVE "test cmd locate lazy the village is found before any chunk was made" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE WS-LAZY-V(1:12) TO TL-OBSERVED
     MOVE "The nearest " TO TL-EXPECTED
     PERFORM CHECK-S
     MOVE "locate structure minecraft:stronghold" TO WS-LINE
     CALL "TEST-RUN-CONSOLE" USING WS-LINE WS-LAZY-S
     MOVE "test cmd locate lazy the stronghold is found before any chunk was made" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE WS-LAZY-S(1:12) TO TL-OBSERVED
     MOVE "The nearest " TO TL-EXPECTED
     PERFORM CHECK-S
     MOVE "locate structure minecraft:village_plains" TO WS-LINE
     CALL "TEST-RUN-CONSOLE" USING WS-LINE WS-LAZY-T

*>   The same world again, its setup run by hand first: the same answers.
     CALL "TEST-OPEN-WORLD" USING CORE-SETTINGS
     CALL "GEN-WORLD-SETUP"
     CALL "OVB-BUILD"
     CALL "STRUCT-POSSIBLE-BUILD"
     MOVE "locate structure #minecraft:village" TO WS-LINE
     CALL "TEST-RUN-CONSOLE" USING WS-LINE WS-TEXT
     MOVE "test cmd locate lazy the village answer is the one of a world after its setup" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE WS-TEXT TO TL-OBSERVED
     MOVE WS-LAZY-V TO TL-EXPECTED
     PERFORM CHECK-S
     MOVE "locate structure minecraft:stronghold" TO WS-LINE
     CALL "TEST-RUN-CONSOLE" USING WS-LINE WS-TEXT
     MOVE "test cmd locate lazy the stronghold answer is the one of a world after its setup" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE WS-TEXT TO TL-OBSERVED
     MOVE WS-LAZY-S TO TL-EXPECTED
     PERFORM CHECK-S
     MOVE "locate structure minecraft:village_plains" TO WS-LINE
     CALL "TEST-RUN-CONSOLE" USING WS-LINE WS-TEXT
     MOVE "test cmd locate lazy a single village structure answer is the one of a world after its setup" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE WS-TEXT TO TL-OBSERVED
     MOVE WS-LAZY-T TO TL-EXPECTED
     PERFORM CHECK-S

*>   A saved world opened again by a new process: no spawn search runs (the world exists), so nothing of the setup has run (the climate points are cleared
*>   here the way a new process starts, the generator setup and the possible sets are cleared by the open).
     CALL "CORE-SAVE"
     CALL "CORE-WORLD-OPEN" USING WS-WORLD CORE-SETTINGS WS-CREATED
     MOVE 0 TO CL-COUNT
     DISPLAY "STATE reopened setup-done " GQ-SETUP-DONE " cl-count " CL-COUNT " poss-done " SD-POSS-DONE " created " WS-CREATED
     MOVE "locate structure #minecraft:village" TO WS-LINE
     CALL "TEST-RUN-CONSOLE" USING WS-LINE WS-TEXT
     MOVE "test cmd locate lazy a world loaded from disk answers the village like a world after its setup" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE WS-TEXT TO TL-OBSERVED
     MOVE WS-LAZY-V TO TL-EXPECTED
     PERFORM CHECK-S
     MOVE "locate structure minecraft:village_plains" TO WS-LINE
     CALL "TEST-RUN-CONSOLE" USING WS-LINE WS-TEXT
     MOVE "test cmd locate lazy a world loaded from disk answers a single village structure like a world after its setup" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE WS-TEXT TO TL-OBSERVED
     MOVE WS-LAZY-T TO TL-EXPECTED
     PERFORM CHECK-S
     STOP RUN.

 CHECK-N.
     MOVE "N" TO TL-MODE
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE "T" TO TL-MODE.

 CHECK-S.
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT.
 END PROGRAM TEST-CMD-LOCATE-LAZY.

 COPY CORETEST.
 COPY CMDTEST.
